# nvme-cli configuration template
#
# This package provides command-line utilities for managing NVMe devices.
# It is a leaf utility package and does not run as a persistent service.
# Therefore, it has no network bindings, no port requirements, and no
# service capabilities to offer or consume in a cluster topology.
#
# The template is retained here as a self-documenting placeholder
# to satisfy structural requirements of the role engine, but it
# contains no actionable directives.

# No configuration directives are required or supported by nvme-cli.
# Users should invoke `nvme-cli` commands directly (e.g., via cron or scripts).
